1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,760
The bank has known Aziz for six years.

2
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:06,576
He has a salary card there, and a deposit that he often forgets about.

3
00:00:06,626 --> 00:00:08,640
heeyID has known him for one week.

4
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:12,512
Are they talking about the same man?

5
00:00:12,562 --> 00:00:19,208
In Lesson 18, the phone check gave Aziz the status Confirmed, and with it level two and a trusted phone.

6
00:00:19,258 --> 00:00:26,840
This lesson takes the last step of the step-up: linking, the answer to one question, is this proofed person a customer of the bank?

7
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:29,024
Two records, in two systems.

8
00:00:29,074 --> 00:00:36,128
The heeyID person record is about identity: the phone number, the password, the level and the verified identity.

9
00:00:36,178 --> 00:00:40,616
The bank's customer record is about money: accounts, cards and products.

10
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:43,664
Linking connects them with one thin thread.

11
00:00:43,714 --> 00:00:51,056
When the status becomes Confirmed, the platform sends one value to the bank's customer lookup: the personal identification number.

12
00:00:51,106 --> 00:00:53,240
Nothing else about Aziz leaves.

13
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:55,208
The lookup has five answers.

14
00:00:55,258 --> 00:01:01,520
Found and active: the platform attaches the bank customer identifier, and the link state is Linked.

15
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:03,392
That is Aziz's answer today.

16
00:01:03,442 --> 00:01:10,712
Not found: the link state is Not linked, and the platform sends an event that the bank can use to start its own account opening.

17
00:01:10,762 --> 00:01:14,384
Opening an account is a process of the bank, not of the platform.

18
00:01:14,434 --> 00:01:20,504
Found but closed or blocked: the link state is Refused, and an operator gets a case.

19
00:01:20,554 --> 00:01:24,248
More than one found: also Refused, and also a case.

20
00:01:24,298 --> 00:01:28,400
And no answer within the configured timeout: the link state is Pending.

21
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:32,120
The platform keeps the bank customer identifier, and nothing more.

22
00:01:32,170 --> 00:01:39,152
If the lookup answers with accounts, products or balances, the platform deletes those fields before any other step.

23
00:01:39,202 --> 00:01:41,072
A reference, never a copy.

24
00:01:41,122 --> 00:01:44,944
Why so strict?

25
00:01:44,994 --> 00:01:50,656
A copy is old on the day it is made, and every copy is one more place to leak from.

26
00:01:50,706 --> 00:01:55,792
The lookup answer may also carry a name and a date of birth, only for comparison.

27
00:01:55,842 --> 00:02:00,208
The bank's records spell Aziz's family name in an older Latin spelling.

28
00:02:00,258 --> 00:02:04,864
The platform records a comparison note on Aziz, and on the link event.

29
00:02:04,914 --> 00:02:09,640
The difference alone does not stop the step-up, and it does not change the link state.

30
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:14,032
Now the rule that, I think, a tired developer will most want to break.

31
00:02:14,082 --> 00:02:16,864
There is no operation that links by phone number.

32
00:02:16,914 --> 00:02:21,088
Not in the gateway, not in the admin panel, and not for an operator.

33
00:02:21,138 --> 00:02:24,472
The lookup accepts only a personal identification number.

34
00:02:24,522 --> 00:02:27,216
Why?

35
00:02:27,266 --> 00:02:31,320
Because mobile operators give old phone numbers to new persons.

36
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:36,240
The number that Aziz used at university may belong to a stranger next year.

37
00:02:36,290 --> 00:02:40,704
A link by phone would one day attach that stranger to Aziz's deposit.

38
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:44,208
A phone number is a contact channel, not an identifier.

39
00:02:44,258 --> 00:02:48,080
What if the lookup is down?

40
00:02:48,130 --> 00:02:53,720
Imagine that Aziz is confirmed on a night when the bank's customer system is in maintenance.

41
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:55,592
His link state is Pending.

42
00:02:55,642 --> 00:03:01,592
The platform tries again at the configured interval, during the configured period, and records each result.

43
00:03:01,642 --> 00:03:08,864
After the period, the state becomes Refused, with the reason: lookup not available, and an operator gets a case.

44
00:03:08,914 --> 00:03:11,936
Meanwhile, Aziz keeps his access grant.

45
00:03:11,986 --> 00:03:15,608
His level is two, and the link is a separate fact.

46
00:03:15,658 --> 00:03:21,464
The mobile bank reads the link state in the identity summary, and decides which banking functions to show.

47
00:03:21,514 --> 00:03:23,768
A refused link can still end well.

48
00:03:23,818 --> 00:03:29,600
An operator who resolves the case can enter the bank customer identifier, after the bank checks it.

49
00:03:29,650 --> 00:03:35,600
The link becomes Linked, with the mark set by operator, and with the operator, the time and the reason.

50
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:45,176
To recap: one value goes out, one identifier comes back, each answer has its state, a mismatched name gets a note, and nothing ever links by phone.

51
00:03:45,226 --> 00:03:49,544
Aziz's step-up is complete: level two, confirmed and linked.

52
00:03:49,594 --> 00:03:51,488
Module four ends here.

53
00:03:51,538 --> 00:03:54,272
From now on, his phone carries all of this.

54
00:03:54,322 --> 00:03:58,016
But what exactly makes a phone trusted, and what does the app keep on it?

55
00:03:58,066 --> 00:04:00,248
Next: the trusted device.
